# "This land enters tapped." and the bounced Plains does not give a second land drop (CR 305.2): on turn 3, after the Chancery returns the Plains, the Chancery cannot be tapped for mana
# (it is tapped) and the Plains cannot be played again (refusals). On turn 5 the same two actions are fine (the positive controls): the Plains is played and the Chancery taps for {W}{U}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Azorius Chancery
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Azorius Chancery.Play
Bot1.Choose(Plains)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Azorius Chancery.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Azorius Chancery.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {W}{U}

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Battlefield = Azorius Chancery; Plains
